Python packages for the workspace's python3
  setup/python.py downloads these into state/python: Pyodide's builds from
  the jsDelivr CDN at the installed Pyodide's version, and pure-Python
  wheels from PyPI. Each keeps its own license, as its wheel's metadata
  states:

    et-xmlfile 2.0.0               MIT
    lxml 6.0.2                     BSD-3-Clause
    numpy 2.4.6                    BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib
                                   AND CC0-1.0
    opencv-python 4.11.0.86        Apache-2.0
    openpyxl 3.1.5                 MIT
    pandas 3.0.2                   BSD-3-Clause
    pillow 12.2.0                  MIT-CMU
    pyarrow 22.0.0                 Apache-2.0
    pymupdf 1.27.2.2               AGPL-3.0, or Artifex's commercial license
    pyodide-unix-timezones 1.0.0   MIT
    pypdf 6.21.2                   BSD-3-Clause
    python-dateutil 2.9.0.post0    Apache-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause, dual
    python-docx 1.2.0              MIT
    python-pptx 1.0.2              MIT
    pytz 2026.1.post1              MIT
    six 1.17.0                     MIT
    typing-extensions 4.15.0       PSF-2.0
    tzdata 2025.3                  Apache-2.0
    xlsxwriter 3.3.0               BSD-2-Clause

  pymupdf's AGPL applies to whoever conveys it. vfs-bench-2 only downloads
  it for local runs and never redistributes it.


